; Thompson M1A1 placeholder viewmodel, assembled from primitives.
; Local space: barrel fires along -Z, +Y up. Roughly life-size (~0.81m long).
;
; The wartime M1A1, not the M1928: plain barrel with no cooling fins and no
; Cutts compensator, a straight box magazine rather than a drum, a horizontal
; wooden forend in place of the vertical foregrip, and the bolt handle on the
; receiver's right flank.
[gd_scene load_steps=22 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/weapon.gd" id="1_weapon"]

; Parkerised olive-drab rather than blued: the M1A1 was a wartime austerity
; build and photographs distinctly greener than the shotgun or the Garand.
